  "result": "I fixed the clamping for open bounds on `IntRange`. I didn't run the tests or try it with an actual option.\n\nIn `IntRange._clamp` (`src/click/types.py`), the open-bound case moved the value the wrong way. `convert` passes `dir=1` for the lower bound and `dir=-1` for the upper bound. The old code did `bound - dir`, so clamping to an open lower bound gave `min - 1` and an open upper bound gave `max + 1`. Both are outside the range. It now does `bound + dir`, which gives `min + 1` and `max - 1`.\n\nFor example, `IntRange(0, 10, min_open=True, max_open=True, clamp=True)` now returns 1 for an input of -5 and 9 for an input of 50.\n\nClosed bounds were already correct. `FloatRange` rejects clamping with open bounds, so it wasn't affected.",
